{"id": "300afa28-e460-444f-911e-caeead6002cf", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T14:16:59.872979", "source": "user", "parent_id": "af98adb1-f886-4a81-89fb-c4767183dc19", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Welcome. This is a design-only task: we need a final experiment design (with rationale, controls, analysis plan, and feasibility) answering how autocorrelation analysis can be used to identify the optimal cycle length for CycleNet in time series forecasting. Experimental execution is not required. For this first step, please do NOT produce the full design yet. Instead:\\n\\n1. Inspect the available project materials (e.g., read track.md in /workspace and list any other relevant files/notes) and summarize what source-supported setup details they provide for CycleNet and for the autocorrelation analysis.\\n2. Propose a high-level experimental approach (sketch only): the datasets/benchmarks you intend to use, how CycleNet's cycle length is configured and varied, and how autocorrelation of the inputs would be computed and linked to a chosen cycle length. Keep it at the level of a proposed plan, not the final write-up.\\n3. Enumerate the consequential assumptions and uncertainties you are making (e.g., definition of \\\"optimal\\\" cycle length — predictive accuracy vs. autocorrelation peak, seasonality granularity, dataset-specific periodicities, CycleNet configuration defaults), so we can agree on them before the main design work.\\n\\nDo not run or claim any experiment. Report what you find from inspection and your proposed approach, along with the open assumptions.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How can we use autocorrelation analysis to identify the optimal cycle length for CycleNet in time series forecasting?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
