Assumptions, uncertainties, and provenance\\n\\n**Assumptions (fixed requirements are marked):** (A1) optimal = min validation MSE per (dataset, pred_len) (fixed requirement). (A2) ACF computed on standardized/detrended training split with threshold+separation peak detection (requirement). (A3) single dominant cycle per run for multi-periodic series (requirement). (A4) only cycle_len varies; all else fixed (requirement). Remaining assumptions are To-Confirm: exact official per-dataset cycle_len/time_enc_dim/backbone/hyperparameters; dataset sampling-rate map; official pred_len set; official split scheme.\\n\\n**Uncertainties to be resolved at execution:** ACF peak may not coincide with predictive optimum at long horizons (exactly what is measured); multi-periodic dominance (daily vs weekly) ambiguity; whether validation-based optimum differs materially from test optimum; effect of the detrending choice on peaks; channel-pooling choice for multivariate ACF.\\n\\n**Provenance:** the only source-supported material in this workspace is task.json stating this is a design-only task; all CycleNet/dataset specifics above are from public knowledge of the CycleNet (NeurIPS 2024, ACAT-SCUT/CycleNet) paper/repo and are explicitly To-Confirm. No experiment was run; no numeric results are claimed beyond the prespecified decision thresholds (coverage@1 \\u2265 0.6, median lift \\u2264 1%, coverage@5 \\u2265 0.8), which are design choices, not outcomes.\", \"evidence\": \"Inspection evidence: /workspace contains only task.json; documents.track.md = 'Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.' No CycleNet code, no track.md file, no datasets. Environment: Python 3.14.4; numpy/scipy/pandas not installed (import errors); network disabled; GPU disabled (224 CPU cores); datasets=[]. Therefore the design is grounded in the public CycleNet paper/repo (RCM + cycle-aware time indices; DLinear/PatchTST backbones; ETT/Electricity/Traffic/Weather/PEMS/Solar benchmarks), all marked To-Confirm. Design-only; no experiment run; decision thresholds (coverage@1\\u22650.6, median lift\\u22641%, coverage@5\\u22650.8) are prespecified analytic criteria, not observed results.\", \"assumptions\": [\"Optimal cycle length = the cycle_len minimizing mean validation MSE per (dataset, pred_len); test MSE is confirmatory only.\", \"ACF computed on standardized/detrended training split; candidates = local maxima above max(0.3, 2/sqrt(T)) with minimum separation; top-k (k=5) ranked; FFT periodogram as cross-check.\", \"Single dominant cycle assumed per run for multi-periodic series (daily vs weekly ambiguity measured, not assumed away).\", \"Only cycle_len varies across sweeps; all other hyperparameters, 7:1:2 splits, and >=3 seeds fixed.\", \"CycleNet configured per official ACAT-SCUT/CycleNet single-integer cycle_len + RCM with cycle-aware time indices.\", \"Execution requires a provisioned environment with the official repo, datasets, and a working torch stack; absent in this sandbox (network disabled, no deps, no data, no GPU).\", \"Exact per-dataset defaults (cycle_len, time_enc_dim, backbone, sampling-rate map, official pred_len set) are To-Confirm from the official repo/paper and recorded in a setup table before execution.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Exact official defaults per dataset and whether the chosen backbone (DLinear/PatchTST) reproduces the published schedule.\", \"Whether the ACF-dominant period coincides with the predictive optimum, especially at long horizons where the cyclical component matters more \\u2014 this is the measured effect, not an assumed equality.\", \"Multi-periodic dominance: hourly data with both daily (24) and weekly (168) cycles may yield multiple strong ACF peaks; which one is optimal may vary.\", \"Detrending/no-detrending and per-channel vs pooled ACF choices may shift detected peaks; handled as robustness variants.\", \"Validation-based optimum vs test optimum; and whether the prespecified coverage thresholds are met (to be reported, not claimed).\"]}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
